# ClariFin_OS — Canonical .gitignore
#
# ONLY committed artifacts are C64 forensic evidence and provenance documents.
# Everything else is either generated, cached, or IDE-local state.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEPENDENCIES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
node_modules/
.kilo/node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BUILD OUTPUTS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
clarinfin_verification.egg-info/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CACHE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.turbo/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
memory-bank/
test-results/
dependency-reports/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ENVIRONMENT & SECRETS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.env
.env*.local
.env.production

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LOGS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*.log
npm-debug.log
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OS FILES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# IDE (keep root-level configs, ignore IDE-specific)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.vscode/
.idea/
.sublime-*
.cursor/
.kilo/plans/
.kilo/worktrees/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PYTHON VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENTS
# CANONICAL: Only repository-root .venv is allowed.
# backend/venv and backend/.venv are FORBIDDEN (M9-C42.5).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.venv/
backend/venv/
backend/.venv/
venv/
env/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PYTHON CACHE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATABASE & DATA
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/
uploads/
# Exception: backend/src/data/ is source, never local data
!backend/src/data/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MISCELLANEOUS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.vercel
.expo/
.temp/
temp/
tmp/
unrelated/
servers/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MUTATION TESTING
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
backend/mutants/
backend/run_mutmut_patched.sh
.mutmut-cache/
mutants/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# VERIFICATION PIPELINE GENERATED
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RUNTIME GENERATED — POLICY
#
# Policy: the regenerable bulk of runtime output is ignored; milestone
# certification evidence and the contract/reference artifacts below stay
# version-controlled.
#
# Correction history. The first pass at this policy excluded the whole subtree
# and re-included a hand-picked list of six milestone directories (151 files),
# on the reasoning that anything else was regenerable output. That was wrong,
# and CI proved it: 90 runtime tests failed with missing evidence — m9-c55
# certification artifacts, m9-c42.28/.29/.30 baselines and scenarios, m9-c48
# governance records, and a family of top-level certification JSONs. Those tests
# read that material as *inputs*, and no bootstrap step regenerates it. The
# repository also keeps hand-written scenario and certification scripts under
# runtime/generated/ (38 .py files) which the tests execute by path.
#
# So the line is not "canonical directory vs everything else". It is:
#
#   ignored  = bulk regenerable output, identified by what it IS
#   tracked  = milestone evidence, baselines, scenarios, certification records
#              and the scripts that produce or check them
#
# The ignored set is expressed as a type filter rather than an allow-list,
# because every excluded class is a build artifact with an unambiguous
# signature, and because an allow-list silently swallows anything a new
# milestone commits.
#
# Before this rule ~4,568 files were tracked, of which 2,870 were diffs, logs and
# caches. Those are still untracked; the ~2,680 evidence and script files are
# tracked again.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The ignored set is expressed purely as type filters. The subtree itself is
# never excluded, because git does not descend into an excluded directory — a
# `runtime/generated/` rule plus `!` exceptions would make every exception
# unreachable for any *new* file, which is exactly the trap the first attempt at
# this policy fell into. Ignoring by file signature instead means the ~2,680
# evidence and script files stay tracked, an unlisted artifact is tracked by
# default, and only the bulk is ever ignored.
#
# ── Regenerable bulk: mutation survivor diffs ──
# One .diff per surviving mutant, rewritten by every mutation campaign. They
# prove nothing across commits and dominate the subtree at 2,038 files.
*.diff

# ── Regenerable bulk: logs and captured command output ──
# Per-run command output; 832 files, all rewritten.
*.log
*.log.txt
*.stdout
*.stderr
runtime/generated/logs/

# ── Regenerable bulk: caches, bytecode and mutation scratch space ──
__pycache__/
*.pyc
runtime/generated/**/mutants/
runtime/generated/**/.mutmut-cache/
runtime/generated/**/symbol-cache.json
runtime/generated/**/symbol-test-map.json

# Per-process pytest progress records (one pair per test session, rewritten as
# the session runs — local diagnostic evidence, never committed).
runtime/generated/verification-progress/

# ── Regenerable bulk: runtime snapshots ──
# Cached platform/health snapshots, rewritten on every read. Their TTL and
# build cost are managed in runtime/platform/cache.py.
runtime/generated/platform/snapshot.json

# ── Regenerable bulk: per-run execution scratch ──
# runtime/generated/execution/ is the executor's per-run results directory
# (runtime/foundation/verification/executor.py:50) — per-task stdout/stderr and
# per-task snapshots, rewritten by every verification run. CI preserves it by
# *uploading* it as a workflow artifact, which is what a run's evidence is for;
# versioning it in Git would commit one run's scratch into the next. The files
# are named after task ids, which contain '::', and upload-artifact rejects
# ':' in a path — so tracking them also broke Backend and Frontend Verification
# on any run that produced a namespaced task id such as ci::parity::money.
runtime/generated/execution/
runtime/generated/mutation-cache/
runtime/generated/mutation-shards/
# runtime/generated/ai-runs/ is the AI orchestrator's per-run state, one
# JSON document per run, rewritten by every orchestrated run.
runtime/generated/ai-runs/

# ── Contract / reference artifacts ──
# frontend/generated/openapi-current.json is the committed API contract
# baseline that the API Contract Integrity gate diffs against
# (runtime/foundation/verification/api_contracts/gate.py), and
# toolchain-lock.json pins the frontend toolchain contract. These are
# inputs, not output, and are therefore version-controlled.
!frontend/generated/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GENERATED STATE THAT ESCAPED ITS ROOT
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Several tools write through cwd-relative paths, so a run started from
# a subdirectory materialises a nested copy of the tree (a run from
# backend/ produced backend/runtime/generated/). These are runtime
# state by definition and must never be committed.
runtime/runtime/generated/
backend/runtime/generated/
frontend/runtime/generated/
.github/backend/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GENERATED ARTIFACTS (keep only specific ones)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Backend test generated artifacts — regenerated deterministically by
# .github/scripts/run_fast_checks.sh (tools/development/check_coverage.py)
# from tracked inputs on every run, including a clean checkout.
backend/tests/generated/

# M9-C71 — mutation-measurement trust.
# The sentinel sink is per-run append-only execution evidence regenerated by
# every mutation shard; committing it would add a file that changes on every
# campaign and proves nothing about the code.
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/*-sentinel-sink.jsonl
# mutmut-generated mutants and bytecode caches are build artifacts.
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/mutants/
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/.mutmut-cache/
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/__pycache__/
